    <mxCell id="cDel" value="DeleteEventCommand

- _ev:MapEventDto
Execute→DeleteEvent
Undo→AddEvent" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="900" y="470" width="310" height="160" as="geometry"/>
    </mxCell>
    <mxCell id="cRep" value="ReplaceEventCommand

- _oldEv:MapEventDto
- _newEv:MapEventDto
Execute→ReplaceEvent(old,new)
Undo→ReplaceEvent(new,old)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="560" y="520" width="310" height="200" as="geometry"/>
    </mxCell>
    <mxCell id="note" value="Why command pattern?
• Every edit becomes an object.
• Undo/redo is symmetric and reliable.
• PersistMap() can autosave based on state
  (sample map always; user maps only after first manual save).
• Rendering stays simple: after Execute/Undo
  I just RequestViewportRender()." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="40" y="480" width="420" height="260" as="geometry"/>
    </mxCell>
